{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols"]]},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"ColoringModule","relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"]}],"externalID":"s:e:s:14GraphProtocols0A0P14ColoringModuleE04edgeC0AD04EdgeC0VyxGyF","fragments":[{"text":"extension","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Graph","kind":"identifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P"}],"extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","title":"Graph","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Graph","kind":"identifier"}],"symbolKind":"extension","role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Extended Protocol"},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Instance-Methods","title":"Instance Methods","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/bipartiteEdgeColoring()","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/chromaticNumber()","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/edgeColoring()","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/greedyColoring(order:)","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/greedyColoring(strategy:)","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/greedyColoring(strategy:presetColor:)","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/greedyEdgeColoring()","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/isEdgeColoring(_:)","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/isVertexColoring(_:)","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/lexicographicallyFirstMinimumColoring()","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/minimumColoring()"]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/graphprotocols\/graph"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"extension","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","text":"Graph","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P"}]}]}],"references":{"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/GraphProtocols/Graph/greedyColoring(strategy:presetColor:)":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"greedyColoring"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"strategy"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"ColoringStrategy","preciseIdentifier":"s:14ColoringModule0A8StrategyO"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"presetColor"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"},{"kind":"text","text":"?) -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Coloring","preciseIdentifier":"s:14ColoringModule0A0V"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The greedy colouring with some colours fixed in advance (rustworkx","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"graph_greedy_color(preset_color_fn=)"},{"text":"): ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"presetColor"},{"text":" gives a vertex’s colour, or nil to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"leave it to the strategy. Preset vertices keep their colours and count as coloured from the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"start; the others are coloured as by ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"greedyColoring(strategy:)"},{"text":", each taking the least","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"colour no coloured neighbour has. The orders of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".largestFirst"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".smallestLast"},{"text":" and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"connected sequential strategies are those of the whole graph with the preset vertices","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"skipped (rustworkx’s largest first: whole-graph degrees, preset vertices left out);","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"DSatur counts preset colours in saturation from the start (rustworkx’s saturation);","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".independentSet"},{"text":"‘s class k starts without the neighbours of the vertices preset to k","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(rustworkx’s independent set); ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".coloredNeighbors"},{"text":" counts preset neighbours as coloured and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"takes its first vertex from its heap. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"colorCount"},{"text":" is one more than the greatest colour,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"so preset colours may leave some colours unused. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"presetColor"},{"text":" is called once per vertex,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"text":" order. The strategy’s time, plus O(n + m) to check the presets.","type":"text"}],"title":"greedyColoring(strategy:presetColor:)","url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/graphprotocols\/graph\/greedycoloring(strategy:presetcolor:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/greedyColoring(strategy:presetColor:)","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol"},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","role":"symbol","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Graph"}],"abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/graphprotocols\/graph","title":"Graph","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"extension"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P","text":"Graph"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule":{"kind":"symbol","title":"ColoringModule","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule","role":"collection","type":"topic","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule"},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/GraphProtocols/Graph/greedyColoring(strategy:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/greedyColoring(strategy:)","role":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A greedy colouring of the simple graph (self-loops ignored, parallel edges once): each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex in the strategy’s order takes the least colour none of its already coloured"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"neighbours has. NetworkX "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"greedy_color(G, strategy)"},{"type":"text","text":", the same colours on simple graphs for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".largestFirst"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".saturationLargestFirst"},{"type":"text","text":", and for the others wherever NetworkX’s set"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"iteration is ascending (NetworkX counts a self-loop in degrees, and its smallest last"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"raises on one); igraph "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertex_coloring_greedy"},{"type":"text","text":" for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".coloredNeighbors"},{"type":"text","text":"; Boost"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sequential_vertex_coloring"},{"type":"text","text":" in the strategy’s order; rustworkx "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"graph_greedy_color"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Colours are first-fit numbers, not renumbered: colour 0 goes to the first vertex coloured."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"At most Δ + 1 colours ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".smallestLast"},{"type":"text","text":": degeneracy + 1). O(n + m) for largest first and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"connected sequential, O((n + m) log n) for smallest last, DSatur and colored neighbours,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"O(χ (n + m) log n) for independent set."}],"url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/graphprotocols\/graph\/greedycoloring(strategy:)","title":"greedyColoring(strategy:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"greedyColoring","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"strategy","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14ColoringModule0A8StrategyO","text":"ColoringStrategy","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14ColoringModule0A0V","text":"Coloring","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/GraphProtocols/Graph/isEdgeColoring(_:)":{"abstract":[{"text":"Whether every two edges with a common end have different colours: parallel edges, which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"share both ends, and a self-loop and any other edge at its vertex (igraph","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"is_edge_coloring"},{"text":"). Any Ints count as colours. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"color"},{"text":" is called once per edge, in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges"},{"text":" order. O(n + m), plus one hash per edge when the colours are not small","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"non-negative numbers.","type":"text"}],"title":"isEdgeColoring(_:)","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/isEdgeColoring(_:)","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/graphprotocols\/graph\/isedgecoloring(_:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"isEdgeColoring","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"((","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edges","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Index","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/GraphProtocols/Graph/lexicographicallyFirstMinimumColoring()":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/lexicographicallyFirstMinimumColoring()","role":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The lexicographically first minimum colouring of the simple graph: on each connected"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"component, of all its colourings with its own chromatic number of colours, the one whose"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"colour vector (in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order) is lexicographically least, Khuller and Vazirani’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"lexicographically first k-colouring (1991) with k = the component’s χ. So within a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"component colours appear in order of first use, colour classes are numbered by their least"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex, a bipartite component is coloured by its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"bipartition()"},{"type":"text","text":" sides (left 0), and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"colorCount == chromaticNumber()"},{"type":"text","text":". Components are not coupled: a bipartite one keeps two"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"colours beside a triangle."}],"url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/graphprotocols\/graph\/lexicographicallyfirstminimumcoloring()","title":"lexicographicallyFirstMinimumColoring()","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"lexicographicallyFirstMinimumColoring","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Coloring","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14ColoringModule0A0V"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An undirected graph: a finite set of vertices and a finite collection of undirected edges"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"between them. Kept apart from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":": an undirected graph is not a symmetric directed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one, and no type is both. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"directed"},{"type":"text","text":" views it as one when an algorithm needs arcs."}],"kind":"symbol","title":"Graph","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/graph","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Graph","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Graph","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/GraphProtocols":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols","role":"collection","type":"topic","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/graphprotocols","title":"GraphProtocols","kind":"symbol"},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/GraphProtocols/Graph/bipartiteEdgeColoring()":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An edge colouring with exactly Δ colours, Δ counting parallel edges, on a bipartite graph"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(König’s theorem; rustworkx "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"graph_bipartite_edge_color"},{"type":"text","text":"), or nil when the graph is not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"bipartite ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"findOddCycle()"},{"type":"text","text":" gives the witness; a self-loop makes it not bipartite)."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Parallel edges are fine. Edges in position order: each takes the least colour free at its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"end with the lesser vertex index, after the alternating path of that colour and the least"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"colour free at the other end is flipped from the other end, when the two differ there."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"O(m · (n + Δ)) time, O(n + m) memory."}],"kind":"symbol","title":"bipartiteEdgeColoring()","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/bipartiteEdgeColoring()","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/graphprotocols\/graph\/bipartiteedgecoloring()","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"bipartiteEdgeColoring","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EdgeColoring","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14ColoringModule04EdgeA0V"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">?","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/GraphProtocols/Graph/greedyColoring(order:)":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"First fit in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"order"},{"type":"text","text":" on the simple graph: each vertex in turn takes the least colour none of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its already coloured neighbours has (Boost "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sequential_vertex_coloring(g, order, color)"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"JGraphT "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GreedyColoring"},{"type":"text","text":", NetworkX "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"greedy_color"},{"type":"text","text":" with a callable strategy). A shuffled"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" is NetworkX’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"random_sequential"},{"type":"text","text":". At most Δ + 1 colours. O(n + m) after one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"lookup per vertex."}],"kind":"symbol","title":"greedyColoring(order:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/greedyColoring(order:)","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/graphprotocols\/graph\/greedycoloring(order:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"greedyColoring"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"order"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"some"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Sequence","preciseIdentifier":"s:ST"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa"},{"kind":"text","text":">) -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Coloring","preciseIdentifier":"s:14ColoringModule0A0V"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/GraphProtocols/Graph/chromaticNumber()":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/chromaticNumber()","role":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"The chromatic number χ of the simple graph (self-loops ignored, parallel edges once): the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fewest colours of a proper colouring. 0 for the empty graph, 1 without edges, 2 when","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"bipartite with an edge (BipartiteGraphs’ two-colouring, O(n + m)). Otherwise the greatest","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"over the connected components, each non-bipartite one decided by DSatur branch and bound","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(Brélaz 1979) between a greedy clique and greedy DSatur (Sage ","type":"text"},{"code":"chromatic_number","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", JGraphT","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"BrownBacktrackColoring.getChromaticNumber","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", Mathematica ","type":"text"},{"code":"VertexChromaticNumber","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Exponential in the worst case: Mycielski graphs, whose χ exceeds ω by a lot, are the hard","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ones. The search does not check for task cancellation.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/graphprotocols\/graph\/chromaticnumber()","title":"chromaticNumber()","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"chromaticNumber","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/GraphProtocols/Graph/greedyEdgeColoring()":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A greedy edge colouring of any graph, parallel edges and self-loops included, with at most"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"2Δ − 1 colours: rustworkx "},{"code":"graph_greedy_edge_color","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", the largest-first colouring of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"line graph, with the same colours. Edges by the number of other edges they share an end"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with, most first (a parallel copy counts at both ends, a self-loop meets each other edge at"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its vertex once), ties in position order; each takes the least colour of no edge it shares"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"an end with that is already coloured. A self-loop is one edge at its vertex, as for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"isEdgeColoring(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". O(n + m · Δ) time, O(n + m) memory, without building the line graph."}],"title":"greedyEdgeColoring()","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/greedyEdgeColoring()","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/graphprotocols\/graph\/greedyedgecoloring()","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"greedyEdgeColoring","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EdgeColoring","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14ColoringModule04EdgeA0V"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/GraphProtocols/Graph/isVertexColoring(_:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/isVertexColoring(_:)","role":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Whether ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"color"},{"text":" gives the two ends of every edge different colours (igraph","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"is_vertex_coloring"},{"text":", NetworkX ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"is_coloring"},{"text":"). Self-loops are ignored, as the colourings","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ignore them (NetworkX’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"is_coloring"},{"text":" is false on any loop). Any Ints count as colours, not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"only ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<k"},{"text":". ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"color"},{"text":" is called once per vertex, in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"text":" order. O(n + m).","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/graphprotocols\/graph\/isvertexcoloring(_:)","title":"isVertexColoring(_:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"isVertexColoring","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"((","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/GraphProtocols/Graph/minimumColoring()":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An optimal colouring of the simple graph: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"colorCount == chromaticNumber()"},{"type":"text","text":", with colours"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"numbered by first appearance in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order (the first vertex has colour 0, and each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"colour first appears after the one below it). It is the colouring "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"chromaticNumber()"},{"type":"text","text":"‘s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"search finds, so it costs the same: a bipartite graph gets its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"bipartition()"},{"type":"text","text":" sides (left"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"0), and each other component the colouring that DSatur branch and bound found for it, or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"greedy DSatur’s when that already uses no more colours than another component needs."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Sage "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertex_coloring()"},{"type":"text","text":" and JGraphT "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BrownBacktrackColoring.getColoring"},{"type":"text","text":", which also return"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the optimal colouring their search finds; Mathematica "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FindVertexColoring"},{"type":"text","text":". Deterministic, but which optimal colouring it is depends on the search; for one fixed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"by a rule, see "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lexicographicallyFirstMinimumColoring()"},{"type":"text","text":". Exponential in the worst case, as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"chromaticNumber()"},{"type":"text","text":" is; the search does not check for task cancellation."}],"title":"minimumColoring()","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/minimumColoring()","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/graphprotocols\/graph\/minimumcoloring()","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"minimumColoring","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Coloring","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14ColoringModule0A0V"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/GraphProtocols/Graph/edgeColoring()":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/edgeColoring()","role":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An edge colouring with at most Δ + 1 colours (Vizing’s bound), by Misra and Gries’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"constructive proof (Boost "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edge_coloring"},{"type":"text","text":", rustworkx "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"graph_misra_gries_edge_color"},{"type":"text","text":", with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"their own choices; Sage "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edge_coloring"},{"type":"text","text":"). Edges in position order, each coloured through a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fan at its end with the lesser vertex index, every choice the least colour or vertex"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"available. At least Δ colours always, and Δ + 1 on class-2 graphs (odd cycles, odd complete"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"graphs, Petersen), but sometimes Δ + 1 on class-1 graphs too (K(4)); on a bipartite graph"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"bipartiteEdgeColoring()"},{"type":"text","text":" always gives Δ. O(m · (Δ² + n)) time: a fan has at most Δ"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices, each found among the edges at u, and a path at most n edges. O(n + m) memory."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"For a multigraph ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"digraph.undirected"},{"type":"text","text":" with an antiparallel pair is one), use"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"greedyEdgeColoring()"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/graphprotocols\/graph\/edgecoloring()","title":"edgeColoring()","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"edgeColoring"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"EdgeColoring","preciseIdentifier":"s:14ColoringModule04EdgeA0V"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"kind":"symbol"}}}